.TH CHTTPCLIENT_DO_STREAMING 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttpclient_do_streaming \- perform an HTTP request with a streaming response body
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <chttpclient.h>

ccol_retval_t chttpclient_do_streaming(chttpcli cli,
                                       const chttp_request_t *req,
                                       chttpcli_write_fn write_fn,
                                       void *write_ctx,
                                       int *status_code_out);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Like chttpclient_do, but delivers the response body to write_fn in
chunks as data arrives instead of buffering it.  No chttpcli_response
struct is allocated; response headers are not accessible.

write_fn must return the number of bytes consumed.  Returning less
than len aborts the transfer with a failure.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
cli             Client handle; must not be NULL.
req             Request to execute; must not be NULL.
write_fn        Callback invoked with each body chunk; must not be NULL.
write_ctx       Opaque context pointer passed verbatim to write_fn.
status_code_out Receives the HTTP status code on success; may be NULL.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
Same codes as chttpclient_do.  Additionally,
ccol_http_transfer_aborted is returned when write_fn returns fewer
bytes than len, aborting the transfer.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttpclient_do (3),
.BR chttpclient_do_async_streaming (3),
.BR chttpcli_write_fn (3)
